					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "TRANSPORT INFO\n\nThe most important aspect of the Transport Info node is that it gives you the BPM as a float.\nIn this example we take the BPM and divide it by 400 for our Sine oscillator.\nAs a result, when we change the BPM, the frequency of the oscillator changes and in turn the rate at which the line moves up and down.\n\nAssignment: increase\/decrease the BPM.\n"
					}
				},
