			"5": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "TRANSPORT BEAT\n\nThe most commonly used node for BPM-synchronization is the Transport Beat node.\nThis node outputs a trigger at different musical time intervals like beat or bar.\nTaking the ¼ output guarantees a trigger every beat. \n\nIn this patch we use the Transport Beat node to get a trigger each beat.\nUsing the Attack Release node, we are able to \"pump\" up the shapes on the beat.\n\nAssignment: increase\/decrease the BPM.\n\nNote that there is a Transport Tick node for more complex intervals. \n"
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 681.92388916015625,
					"width": 812.51666259765625,
					"x": -41.564239501953125,
					"y": 261.0526123046875
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffff6a00",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Group",
				"thumbnail_visible": true
			},
			"50": {
				"attributes": {
					"flow": {
						"type": "flow",
